WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.880
If you're just doing AI rather than doing a proper AI transformation,

2
00:00:04.880 --> 00:00:08.320
you're going to see your token costs explode. Here's why.

3
00:00:08.960 --> 00:00:13.920
Running an innovation team, I've seen firsthand that all problem-solving follows the same

4
00:00:13.920 --> 00:00:19.280
basic pattern. You start with a wide range of possibilities, but as you experiment and learn

5
00:00:19.280 --> 00:00:24.880
what works, the space gets narrower until something that started as an open-ended exploration

6
00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:30.080
becomes a predictable, repeatable process. We've measured this with dozens of teams,

7
00:00:30.080 --> 00:00:35.040
and most have somewhere between 50 and 100 distinct tasks they regularly perform.

8
00:00:35.680 --> 00:00:41.360
Each of those tasks has its own little triangle. And because workflows are just groups of tasks,

9
00:00:41.360 --> 00:00:45.680
roles are just groups of workflows, and teams are just groups of roles,

10
00:00:45.680 --> 00:00:50.880
you can call this triangle the general shape of all knowledge work. Frontier models are

11
00:00:50.880 --> 00:00:56.880
really good at this end. But once a task crosses to the other end, you need it to be tight, repeatable,

12
00:00:56.880 --> 00:01:02.240
and predictable. And frontier models aren't just too expensive for that, they're bad at it.

13
00:01:02.240 --> 00:01:06.720
You get better output by encoding your organizational context outside the model,

14
00:01:06.720 --> 00:01:12.160
and using smaller, faster, sometimes even more deterministic software to execute on it.

15
00:01:12.160 --> 00:01:17.680
If your organization is just doing AI, nobody is keeping track of any of this.

16
00:01:17.680 --> 00:01:22.400
You're just taking the same work you do today and throwing the best model you can afford at it.

17
00:01:22.400 --> 00:01:27.760
Don't blame IT for capping your token budget. This is your job to manage, not theirs.

18
00:01:27.760 --> 00:01:33.920
That's why AI transformation is so different from doing AI. It means knowing where every one of

19
00:01:33.920 --> 00:01:40.400
those triangles is, and noticing when each task crosses the threshold from exploration to scalability.

20
00:01:40.400 --> 00:01:45.120
If you're doing this right, token cost per task goes down over time, not up.
